.TH MOQ5\-RELAY.JSON 5 "September 7, 2026" "MOQ5 Relay" "File Formats Manual"
.SH NAME
moq5\-relay.json \- MOQ5 Relay configuration format
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
\fBmoq5\-relay serve \-\-config\fR \fIfile\fR
\fBmoq5\-relay capacity \-\-config\fR \fIfile\fR
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
The file passed to
.BR moq5\-relay (1)
is a JSON object describing the relay's listeners, bounded storage, telemetry,
and authorization policy. There is no implicit file name or search path.
.PP
The parser is strict. Unknown keys, wrong JSON types, unsupported enum values,
negative numbers, duplicate version entries, and values outside their bounds
are errors. The file may be at most 65,535 bytes. Configuration is loaded once
at startup; it is not reloaded after a signal.
.PP
Unless stated otherwise, pool sizes are non\-negative integers. Zero selects
the library default. Entry counts may not exceed 1,048,576 and byte budgets may
not exceed 1 TiB. Cross\-field validation can impose a tighter bound.
.SH TOP-LEVEL OBJECT
The following keys are recognized:
.TP
.B listener
Required object. Configures the raw QUIC listener.
.TP
.B webtransport
Optional object. Configures a second listener carrying MoQ over WebTransport.
.TP
.B admin
Optional object. Configures the loopback admin endpoint.
.TP
.B budgets
Optional object. Sets bounded relay pool and retention capacities.
.TP
.B telemetry
Optional object. Sets observability storage bounds.
.TP
.B logging
Optional object. Selects the output format for the
.B serve
command.
.TP
.B auth
Optional object. Selects the bundled authorization policy. When absent, the
relay allows all requests.
.TP
.B linger_us
Time in microseconds to retain an upstream track after its last subscriber
leaves. Zero, the default, unsubscribes on the next relay tick.
.SH RAW QUIC LISTENER
The
.B listener
object accepts:
.TP
.B transport
Optional string. The only accepted value is
.BR "msquic" .
.TP
.B host
Local address to bind. The default is
.BR "0.0.0.0" .
.TP
.B port
Required integer from 1 through 65535.
.TP
.B cert
Path to the PEM server certificate. Required by
.B serve
but not by
.BR capacity .
.TP
.B key
Path to the PEM private key. Required by
.B serve
but not by
.BR capacity .
.TP
.B versions
Ordered, nonempty array containing unique integers from the set
.BR {18,16} .
The first entry is the server's preferred draft. The default is
.BR [18] .
A single entry creates an exact\-version listener; multiple entries advertise
multiple ALPNs on the same listener.
.TP
.B lanes
Number of independent lock\-domain lanes for this listener, from 1 through 64.
The default is 1. A multi\-lane relay enables the cross\-shard demand plane.
.TP
.B insecure_skip_verify
Optional boolean transport setting. The default is false. It is intended for
controlled demonstrations and tests, not production verification policy.
.SH WEBTRANSPORT LISTENER
The presence of a
.B webtransport
object enables the second listener. The running program must have been built
with wtquic support; otherwise the configuration is refused.
.TP
.B host
Local address to bind. The default is
.BR "0.0.0.0" .
.TP
.B port
Required integer from 1 through 65535.
.TP
.B cert
Required path to this listener's PEM server certificate.
.TP
.B key
Required path to this listener's PEM private key.
.TP
.B lanes
Number of lanes owned by this listener, from 1 through 64. The default is 1.
The sum of
.B listener.lanes
and
.B webtransport.lanes
must not exceed 64.
.TP
.B path
Origin\-form HTTP request path. It must begin with a slash. The default is
.BR "/moq" .
.TP
.B versions
Ordered, nonempty array of unique MoQ drafts from the set
.BR {18,16} .
They are offered as WebTransport subprotocols, with the server's most preferred
draft first. The default is
.BR [18,16] .
.TP
.B profile
WebTransport\-over\-HTTP/3 dialect. This is independent of the MoQ draft in
.BR versions .
The accepted values are:
.RS
.TP
.B current
Current WebTransport\-over\-HTTP/3 signaling. This is the default.
.TP
.B d13_14_compat
Compatibility signaling for the drafts\-13/14 family.
.TP
.B d02_rfc9297_compat
Opt\-in signaling using the draft\-02 request marker with RFC 9297
quarter\-stream\-ID datagrams. The name selects what the listener emits; no
compatibility with any particular client is promised.
.RE
.PP
Selecting
.B d02_rfc9297_compat
requires
.B origin_policy
to be set to something other than
.BR unset .
.TP
.B origin_policy
How the serialized Origin a client presents is authorized. The accepted values
are:
.RS
.TP
.B unset
No Origin rule is applied. This is the default.
.TP
.B allow_any_non_opaque
Any valid tuple origin is accepted; the opaque
.B null
origin is rejected.
.TP
.B allowlist
Only an exact byte match against
.B allowed_origins
is accepted.
.TP
.B allow_any_including_null
Any valid tuple origin is accepted, and so is the opaque
.B null
origin.
.RE
.TP
.B allowed_origins
An array of 1 to 8 exact Origin strings, each at most 320 bytes and 512 bytes
in total including terminators. Accepted only when
.B origin_policy
is
.BR allowlist ,
and required by it: writing a list under any other policy is an error rather
than a value that is ignored, and an empty array is not a list. Entries are
compared byte for byte and are never normalized, so the value must be written
exactly as the client sends it.
.SH ADMIN ENDPOINT
The endpoint is disabled when
.B admin
is absent. The following forms are accepted:
.PP
.nf
"admin": { "enabled": false }
.fi
.PP
or:
.PP
.nf
"admin": {
  "tcp": { "host": "127.0.0.1", "port": 9109 }
}
.fi
.PP
The optional
.B enabled
member is a boolean. Setting it to false is valid only when no endpoint is
configured. Setting it to true does not make the required
.B tcp
object optional.
.PP
The
.B admin.tcp
object accepts:
.TP
.B host
Optional loopback IP literal. The default is
.BR "127.0.0.1" .
IPv4 addresses in 127.0.0.0/8 and the IPv6 loopback address are accepted.
Names, wildcards, IPv4\-mapped IPv6 spellings, and non\-loopback addresses are
refused.
.TP
.B port
Required integer from 1 through 65535.
.PP
The endpoint serves exactly
.BR "GET /metrics" ,
.B "GET /api/v1/info"
and
.BR "GET /api/v1/shards" ;
the two API resources are JSON only. It has no authentication and cannot be
configured for remote binding. For
.B /metrics
a missing
.B Accept
header selects OpenMetrics 1.0; Prometheus text format 0.0.4 is also available
through HTTP content negotiation.
.SH BUDGETS
Every member of
.B budgets
is optional. The direct pool keys are:
.TP
.B max_tracks
Tracks per shard. Default 64.
.TP
.B max_subs
Subscriptions per shard. Default 256.
.TP
.B max_bindings
Session bindings per shard. Default 64. A multi\-shard runtime reserves binding
slots for its managers, so the usable external count may be lower.
.TP
.B max_ns_nodes
Namespace trie nodes per shard. Default 256.
.TP
.B max_ns_subs
Namespace subscriptions per shard. Default 64.
.TP
.B max_intents
Pending intent records per shard. Default 64.
.TP
.B name_intern_bytes
Bytes reserved for interned namespaces and track names. Default 65536.
.TP
.B log_max_subgroups
Subgroups represented per retained group. Default 16.
.TP
.B log_max_objects
Objects represented per retained group. Default 4096.
.TP
.B log_max_cursors
Concurrent retained\-log cursors. Default 64.
.TP
.B log_max_chunk_nodes
Nodes available for chunked open records. Default 8192.
.SS Retained log
The
.B budgets.log
object accepts:
.TP
.B max_groups
Retained groups per track. Default 8.
.TP
.B max_bytes
Retained payload bytes per track. Default 8388608.
.TP
.B max_age_us
Maximum retained group age in microseconds. Zero, the default, disables
age\-based eviction; the count and byte limits still apply.
.SS Cross-shard plane
The
.B budgets.cross_shard
object is accepted at every lane count but allocates cross\-shard machinery
only when the total lane count exceeds one. It accepts:
.TP
.B journal_entries
Namespace journal entries per shard. Zero derives the default from
.BR max_ns_nodes .
.TP
.B mailbox_entries
Control entries per directed shard mailbox. Default 256.
.TP
.B demand_channel_entries
Entries per directed demand channel. Zero derives the default from
.BR pending_demands .
.TP
.B demand_channel_bytes
Data bytes per directed demand channel. Zero derives the default from one
resolved retained\-log payload budget. A nonzero value smaller than one legal
resolved log record is refused.
.TP
.B pending_demands
Remote\-demand table entries per shard. Zero derives the default from
.BR max_tracks .
.TP
.B subgroup_slots
Chunk\-progress slots per demand. Zero selects the binding's resolved open
subgroup limit.
.SH LOGGING
The
.B logging
object accepts:
.TP
.B format
.B text
(the default) or
.BR json .
.IP
.B text
keeps standard output exactly as it is: the readiness lines, the
.B RELAY_RUN_CONFIG_V1
operating\-point row, the post\-join
.B RELAY_LANE_STATS_V3
and
.B RELAY_PAIR_STATS_V1
rows, the stop lines and the capacity ceiling; standard error keeps its
existing diagnostics.
.IP
.B json
applies to
.B serve
only:
.BR capacity ,
.B help
and
.B version
stay text. It makes the serve's standard output carry exactly one JSON
object per line and nothing else. Every row and banner becomes an event:
.B RELAY_READY_V1
(one per listener, one for the admin endpoint, one for the signal contract),
.BR RELAY_RUN_CONFIG_V1 ,
.BR RELAY_LANE_STATS_V3 ,
.B RELAY_PAIR_STATS_V1
and
.BR RELAY_STOP_V1 ,
each with a
.B schema
member naming its versioned record and an
.B elapsed_us
member: microseconds since the log was opened, or
.B null
when the monotonic clock could not supply a trustworthy sample. Numeric
fields keep the names of the text rows; a record the relay cannot supply is
an explicit
.B refused
member, never zeros. The WebTransport readiness event names that listener's
own offered set and its configured
.BR profile ;
naming the configured profile says nothing about what any browser
negotiated. The capacity ceiling and every human message move to standard
error.
.IP
Each event is rendered whole, then written and flushed once. On the first
short write, write error or failed flush the sink stops: no later record is
submitted, and one best\-effort diagnostic goes to standard error. Bytes
already handed to the stream cannot be taken back, so a final partial line
may remain after an I/O failure; a consumer must treat an unterminated last
line as absent. A successful flush hands the bytes to the operating system;
it is not durable delivery to any reader. If standard output is a pipe whose
reader has gone and
.B SIGPIPE
is unblocked at its default disposition, the process terminates on the
write; the relay does not set that signal's disposition or mask. The verify
and measure builds refuse
.B json
for
.BR serve ;
.B capacity
is unaffected.
.SH TELEMETRY
The
.B telemetry
object accepts:
.TP
.B trace_ring_records
Number of recent scalar trace records retained per shard. Zero selects the
library default. The ring is always active; this key changes its bounded depth.
.SH AUTHORIZATION
When the
.B auth
object is absent, the relay installs no authorization hook and allows all
requests. When present,
.B auth.mode
is required.
.SS Allow all
.nf
"auth": { "mode": "allow_all" }
.fi
.PP
The
.B default
and
.B rules
members are not valid in this mode.
.SS Toy policy
The
.B toy
mode is a bounded deterministic action\-and\-namespace policy. It performs no
cryptographic token validation and is not a production identity system.
.TP
.B default
Required fallback decision,
.B allow
or
.BR deny .
.TP
.B rules
Optional array of at most 32 rule objects. Rules are evaluated in array order;
the first match wins.
.PP
Each rule accepts:
.TP
.B action
Required string. One of
.BR client_setup ,
.BR server_setup ,
.BR publish_namespace ,
.BR subscribe_namespace ,
.BR subscribe ,
.BR request_update ,
.BR publish ,
.BR fetch ,
or
.BR track_status .
.TP
.B namespace_prefix
Optional array of zero through eight strings, each at most 64 bytes. An empty
array matches any namespace.
.TP
.B decision
Required value
.B allow
or
.BR deny .
.B defer
cannot be authored in this configuration format.
.TP
.B reason
Optional reason associated with the decision. The default is
.BR policy .
Accepted values are
.BR ok ,
.BR no_token ,
.BR unscoped ,
.BR expired ,
.BR not_yet_valid ,
.BR bad_issuer ,
.BR bad_audience ,
.BR bad_signature ,
and
.BR policy .
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
{
  "listener": {
    "host": "0.0.0.0",
    "port": 4433,
    "versions": [18, 16],
    "lanes": 2,
    "cert": "/etc/moq5\-relay/cert.pem",
    "key": "/etc/moq5\-relay/key.pem"
  },
  "admin": {
    "tcp": { "host": "127.0.0.1", "port": 9109 }
  },
  "budgets": {
    "max_tracks": 256,
    "max_subs": 1024,
    "log": { "max_groups": 8, "max_bytes": 8388608 }
  },
  "telemetry": { "trace_ring_records": 4096 },
  "auth": { "mode": "allow_all" }
}
.fi
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/doc/moq5-relay/examples/relay.json
Example configuration under a conventional system prefix. A distribution or a
custom install prefix may place the documentation elsewhere.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR moq5\-relay (1)
